WARNING:ENOSYS: ENOSYS means 'invalid syscall nr' and nothing else
#68: FILE: drivers/xen/privcmd.c:207:
+		return -ENOSYS;

ENOSYS means that a nonexistent system call was called.
Earlier, it was wrongly used for things like invalid operations on
otherwise valid syscalls.  This should be avoided in new code.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/5eb299021dec23c1a48fa7d9f2c8b794e967766d.1408730669.git.luto@amacapital.net/

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!pages"
#121: FILE: drivers/xen/privcmd.c:334:
+	if (pages == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

WARNING:AVOID_BUG: Avoid crashing the kernel - try using WARN_ON & recovery code rather than BUG() or BUG_ON()
#131: FILE: drivers/xen/privcmd.c:344:
+	BUG_ON(vma->vm_private_data != PRIV_VMA_LOCKED);

BUG() or BUG_ON() should be avoided totally.
Use WARN() and WARN_ON() instead, and handle the "impossible"
error condition as gracefully as possible.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/deprecated.html#bug-and-bug-on

